550:   - id: HS-SEC-004
551:     title: Secure HTTP authentication sessions
552:     normativeStatement: Frontend authentication MUST expose short-lived access tokens only in no-store response bodies, keep rotating refresh tokens exclusively in hardened cookies, protect cookie-authenticated operations from CSRF, and revalidate persistent session and user state on protected requests.
553:     rationale: Browser storage, replayable refresh credentials, ambient cookie authority, and stateless acceptance after revocation each permit avoidable account compromise.
554:     owner: identity-team
555:     status: implemented
556:     risk: critical
